# Every layer that states its remainder quantity in the layer's own unit, beside the magnitude its
# own figures give. One row per examined layer, `violates` where the two differ at any of the three
# points.
#
# A stated quantity is the magnitude
#   The rule: a remainder's `quantity` may be `derived`, and where it is stated it equals
#   `|nameplate - demand|`, the magnitude of the remainder in force. The model already derives that
#   figure from the layer's own demand and nameplate, so a stated quantity is a restatement, and a
#   restatement that differs from what it restates is a contradiction inside one document.
#
# Compared with the remainder in force
#   The magnitude is read from layers/remainder.sqlc through layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc: on
#   a composed layer that owes an exact remainder it is the pivoted `F Φ r - e_n + e_d`, elsewhere
#   the crossed `n - d`. Comparing with the crossed difference of a composed layer's totals would
#   accuse `merge-holding-composition/compute`, whose stated [1414, 2857, 4085.6] is right.
#
# All three points
#   Equality is required at the low, the mode and the high, within 1e-9. A quantity is a range, and
#   a stated range that agrees only at its middle still disagrees with the document's own figures.
#
# What it does not examine
#   A quantity filed as a typed absence states nothing to compare. A quantity in a unit other than
#   the layer's is `not comparable` at arithmetic/filed_remainder.sqlc, which the readiness example
#   pins at zero, so it is left to that site rather than compared across units here.
#
# Probe
#   Change `refutation/compute`'s stated quantity from [0.0, 2.8, 5.0] to [0.0, 2.9, 5.0]. This rule
#   must fire. `examples/witnesses/main.rs` carries that edit.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:quantity against |r| from layers/remainder.sqlc, via layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
           abs(l.qty_low  - l.m_low)  > 1e-9
           OR abs(l.qty_mode - l.m_mode) > 1e-9
           OR abs(l.qty_high - l.m_high) > 1e-9                           AS violates,
           format('stated [%s, %s, %s] against a magnitude of [%s, %s, %s]',
                  l.qty_low, l.qty_mode, l.qty_high, l.m_low, l.m_mode, l.m_high) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc)
    ) l
    WHERE l.qty_low IS NOT NULL
      AND l.qty_unit = l.unit
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'stated_quantity_is_not_the_magnitude'
